    "explanation": "Five-sixths matches ten-twelfths, since multiplying both parts of five-sixths by two produces ten-twelfths exactly. Three-ninths simplifies to one-third when both parts are divided by three, and eight-twelfths simplifies to two-thirds when both parts are divided by four. Four-sixteenths simplifies to one-quarter when both parts are divided by four. Checking every pair this way confirms that each jug fraction has exactly one genuinely equivalent match on the right, even though the two numbers in each pair look quite different at first glance.",
